.TH CHROOTABLE-MANAGER 1 "2026-10-27" "Chrootables" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
chrootable-manager \- create and maintain local Debian image workspaces
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B chrootable-manager
.RI [ command " arguments..." ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
The Bash interface shares the desktop's image store. With no command, it opens
an interactive dashboard. Run mutations and workspace sessions as root.
Read-only commands work without root when the store is readable.
.SH READ-ONLY COMMANDS
.TP
.B --dashboard
Show workspace and storage usage.
.TP
.B --list [--json]
List images as TSV or JSON.
.TP
.B --inspect NAME [--json]
Show image details.
.TP
.B --snapshots NAME
List recovery points, including those of a deleted image.
.TP
.B --profiles
List the minimal, build, python, network, rust, go and web profiles.
.TP
.B --doctor [--json]
Check host readiness and store capacity without installing packages.
JSON output includes individual checks, errors, warnings and storage byte counts.
.TP
.B --capabilities --json
Show versioned profiles, releases, size limits and session options.
.TP
.B --operations [--json]
Inspect durable operation IDs, stages and interrupted work.
.TP
.B --activity
Show recent operation history.
.TP
.B --logs NAME
Show the most recent completed operation log.
.TP
.B --demo [--dashboard]
Show sample workspaces.
.TP
.B --help | --version
Show detailed usage or the version.
.SH CREATE AND USE
.TP
.B --create NAME SIZE_MIB persistent|ephemeral [PROFILE]
Create a sparse image after checking host free space; capacity is not reserved. Sizes range from 512 MiB to 1 TiB.
.TP
.B --archive-sync SUITE [PROFILE...]
Download signed bootstrap and profile packages for offline creation.
.TP
.B --enter NAME [SESSION_OPTIONS]
Open a root shell using the image's default lifecycle.
.TP
.B --enter-isolated NAME [SESSION_OPTIONS]
Open a shell without host network access.
.TP
.B --exec NAME [SESSION_OPTIONS] -- COMMAND [ARG...]
Run a command.
.TP
.B --try NAME [SESSION_OPTIONS] [-- COMMAND [ARG...]]
Use a disposable OverlayFS session regardless of the image lifecycle.
.TP
.B --clone NAME NEW_NAME
Make an independent image copy, using reflinks when available.
.TP
.B --mode NAME persistent|ephemeral
Change the default lifecycle.
.TP
.B --resize NAME SIZE_MIB
Expand an image; shrinking is unsupported.
.TP
.B --export NAME
Create a compressed filesystem archive and print its path.
.TP
.B --import NAME ARCHIVE.tar.gz [SIZE_MIB] [persistent|ephemeral] [PROFILE]
Import a validated .tar.gz archive into a new sparse ext4 image.
.SH SESSION OPTIONS
.TP
.B --isolated
Isolate networking for --exec or --try.
.TP
.B --share /absolute/host/folder
Mount an existing host folder at /shared for the session. The host root cannot be shared.
.TP
.B --read-only
Make the shared folder read-only for ordinary filesystem writes.
.TP
.B --restricted-dev
Expose a minimal /dev instead of the host's device nodes.
.SH RECOVERY AND MAINTENANCE
.TP
.B --snapshot NAME LABEL
Save an offline recovery point.
.TP
.B --restore NAME LABEL --yes
Save current state as a recovery point, then restore a snapshot.
.TP
.B --drop-snapshot NAME LABEL --yes
Permanently remove one snapshot.
.TP
.B --recover-operation ID --yes
Finish an interrupted staged image publication after validating recorded files.
Active operations and unsafe or inconsistent records are refused.
.TP
.B --repair NAME --yes
Force an ext4 filesystem check and repair.
.TP
.B --delete NAME --yes
Delete the image, retaining snapshots and exports.
.TP
.B --prune-logs [KEEP_COUNT] --yes
Remove older completed operation logs while retaining the most recent KEEP_COUNT logs (default 20).
.TP
.B --delete-export FILENAME --yes
Delete a retained export archive from the store exports directory.
.TP
.B --setup
Install missing host prerequisites through the host package manager.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B CHROOTABLE_HOME
Store path; defaults to /var/lib/chrootable-manager.
.TP
.B CHROOTABLE_DEBIAN_SUITE
Debian suite used for creation; defaults to stable.
.TP
.B CHROOTABLE_DEBIAN_MIRROR
Debian mirror; defaults to https://deb.debian.org/debian.
.TP
.B CHROOTABLE_AUTO_INSTALL
Set to 0 to prevent automatic prerequisite installation.
.TP
.B CHROOTABLE_ARCHIVE
Set to 0 to bypass the offline archive.
.SH EXAMPLES
.nf
sudo chrootable-manager --create compiler 4096 persistent build
sudo chrootable-manager --snapshot compiler clean
sudo chrootable-manager --try compiler -- gcc --version
sudo chrootable-manager --restore compiler clean --yes
.fi
.SH NOTES
Workspaces run as host root and are intended for trusted development, not
hostile code. Guest root can alter mounts. Disposable sessions do not undo
writes to shared host folders. Busy images cannot be maintained.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR chrootables-desktop (1),
.BR debootstrap (8),
.BR chroot (8)
